210
00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:51.320
Translucency will give you the true light passing through,

211
00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:52.700
and you would control the roughness,

212
00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.139
you control the opacity amount,

213
00:08:54.139 --> 00:08:56.600
and then you can cloud it out or make it clear.

214
00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.159
And this is not the case here.

215
00:08:58.159 --> 00:09:00.740
We're actually controlling how much of the opacity

216
00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.460
of the light coming through,

217
00:09:02.460 --> 00:09:04.919
but we're not really making it translucent.

218
00:09:04.919 --> 00:09:06.620
So hopefully that makes sense to you.

219
00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:08.500
We're playing with those values.

220
00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.720
And in here, the Fernal Index allows us to complement

221
00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:13.860
that to be able to help with that illusion

222
00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.620
and bend light a bit more in our scene

223
00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:20.179
to be able to actually make it even look more extreme.

224
00:09:20.179 --> 00:09:21.940
Now, if you go down below,

