00:09:51.370 --> 00:09:53.559
So let me show you what I mean.

239
00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:55.440
So if we go down here and we go back

240
00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:56.919
to our instance here,

241
00:09:56.919 --> 00:09:59.360
you're gonna see the effect in real time.

242
00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.509
So I'm gonna go to that subsurface area.

243
00:10:02.509 --> 00:10:06.149
I'm going to increase this subsurface Fernal Control

244
00:10:06.149 --> 00:10:07.710
so the edge here,

245
00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:11.250
we can control how much this value is coming from the edge

246
00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:15.460
of how that light is resting on that object.

247
00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:16.639
Pretty cool.

248
00:10:16.639 --> 00:10:19.299
Now the spec reflection thickness,

249
00:10:19.299 --> 00:10:20.899
if I increase this,

250
00:10:20.899 --> 00:10:23.220
you'll see that we're actually making it

251
00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.080
so that it's kind of doled out.

252
00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:26.139
But if we lower it,

253
00:10:26.139 --> 00:10:28.720
we can actually make it so that we're getting,

254
00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:30.620
it's almost like we're thickening the object.

255
00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:33.340
So we're lessening the amount of light coming through.

256
00:10:33.340 --> 00:10:34.700
But again, this is subsurface.

257
00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:36.980
This isn't opacity,

258
00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:40.179
but the Fernal Index is allowing us to fold the eye

259
00:10:40.179 --> 00:10:41.220
and making you think

260
00:10:41.220 --> 00:10:43.700
that we're controlling the thickness,

261
00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.320
